course: dictionary
lesson: 4462
title: Hardly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Hardly» is a small word with a big job. It means almost not, or only just. «I could hardly see the road in the fog» means I almost could not see it.
explain: Hardly makes a sentence nearly negative, even with no not in it. «She hardly ever eats crisps» means she almost never eats them. Ask yourself: would almost never fit here? If it does, hardly is doing its job.
explain: Hardly can also mean not reasonable. «You can hardly blame him» means it would not be fair to blame him. Use the context around the word to decide which meaning fits.
fact: Hardly means almost not, or only just.
fact: Hardly ever means almost never.
fact: Hardly any means very few, or almost none, as in «hardly any left».
fact: «Hardly» is an adverb, so it tells you more about a verb, such as could see or speak.
fact: «You can hardly blame him» means it is not reasonable to blame him.
exercise: «A flask has two walls with almost no air between them, so heat can hardly cross.» What does hardly mean here? | *Almost not, so heat barely crosses | Completely and easily | Very quickly | Loudly
exercise: Maya says, «We hardly ever go to the seaside.» What does hardly ever mean? | *Almost never | Only at Christmas | Always | Sometimes, every single day
exercise: «There is hardly any juice left in the bottle.» What does hardly any mean? | *Very little, almost none | Some cold juice | A full bottle | Lots and lots
test: «Imagine starting a new school where you hardly speak the language.» What does hardly speak mean? | *Almost do not speak | Speak to the teacher every day | Speak very loudly | Speak it perfectly
test: «You can hardly blame him.» What does this suggest? | He is definitely to blame | He is blame-free and well known | *It would not be reasonable to blame him | Blame him twice as hard
exam: «The emu father sits on the eggs for about 8 weeks, hardly eating.» What does hardly eating mean? | Eating very fast | Eating only at night | Eating a huge meal | *Almost not eating
